      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson-Ulf emphasizes that the clocks transformed precision timekeeping and tests of fundamental physics, with central complementary contributions from Katori and Ye and decades of independent establishment.",
        "response": "I agree that this combination of experimental performance and sustained use makes the case strong. I would retain the caution about separating their foundational advances from later work across the clock community."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth-Eva supports electron recollision, while noting that its theoretical contribution must be distinguished from the attosecond generation and measurement advances recognized by the 2023 prize.",
        "response": "That distinction is important and makes the scope of B009 harder to frame cleanly at this stage. B007 has a clearer basis in independently established measurement methods and a long record of precision gains and applications."
      }
    ],
